{"savedAt":"2026-09-17T22:48:19.882Z","pageCount":120,"model":"restored-from-shots/oct.json","questions":[{"number":"1","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"E","stimulus":"<p>Whatever the general attitude toward Madeline Anderson's 1970 film <i>I Am Somebody</i> and Reginald Hudlin's 1990 film <i>House Party</i> when they were initially released, both films now tend to be regarded quite ______ blank. In 2018, for example, critics for the <i>New York Times</i> praised the former as “galvanizing” and the latter as “exuberant.\"</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>neutrally</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>skeptically</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>favorably</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>strangely</p>"}],"correct":"C","rationale":""},{"number":"2","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"E","stimulus":"<p>The National Heritage Fellowship was created to ______ exceptional folk and traditional artists in the United States. One artist who received the fellowship, the Zydeco musician and singer \"Queen\" Ida Guillory, was chosen for her lifetime contributions to the arts.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>overshadow</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>honor</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>begin</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>distract</p>"}],"correct":"B","rationale":""},{"number":"3","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Broods of periodical cicadas (inch-long winged insects) emerge for six weeks in late spring on a cycle of either 13 or 17 years. In 2024, the emergences of the Great Southern Brood (on a 13-year cycle) and the Northern Illinois Brood (on a 17-year cycle) coincided in the Midwest and Southeast United States, ______ blank that happens only once every 221 years. Sixteen states were covered with a trillion cicadas.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>a convergence</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>an expiration</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>a succession</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>a division</p>"}],"correct":"A","rationale":""},{"number":"4","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"E","stimulus":"<p>Japanese animator and director Hayao Miyazaki often includes fantasy elements in otherwise realistic settings in his movies, but he tends to __________ blank details and exposition about those elements. Miyazaki simply presents fantastical characters and actions with little backstory or explanation, encouraging viewers to embrace the presence of the extraordinary in everyday life.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","keySource":"solved","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>withhold</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>invent</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>combine</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>celebrate</p>"}],"correct":"A","rationale":""},{"number":"5","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Curious about how people visually perceive objects in their dreams, Stephen LaBerge and team recruited lucid dreamers—people aware that they’re dreaming as it’s happening—for a research study. These participants were reliably able to signal when they had entered a dream state; the team then observed participants’ eye movements as they slept. <mark>The smoothness with which participants’ eyes tracked objects in their dreams closely matched how sighted people who are awake visually track objects around them</mark>, suggesting to the team that the brain perceives dream objects as the product of something other than pure imagination.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?</p>","keySource":"solved","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>To offer key evidence that undermines LaBerge and team’s initial hypothesis</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>To show the unexpected result that led LaBerge and team to change the focus of their study</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>To illustrate an important real-world implication of LaBerge and team’s main finding</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>To identify a comparable circumstance that helps justify LaBerge and team’s conclusion</p>"}],"correct":"D","rationale":""},{"number":"6","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"E","stimulus":"<p>Overstrand Hermanus, South Africa, was named a City of Gastronomy by UNESCO in 2019, a title that __________ blank that Overstrand Hermanus has a unique and vibrant food culture worthy of celebration.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","keySource":"solved","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>complains</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>discovers</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>renounces</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>denotes</p>"}],"correct":"D","rationale":""},{"number":"7","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Svante Pääbo and other researchers studying the history of organisms have long utilized ancient DNA—DNA recovered from ancient organic material that has been preserved under natural conditions. However, Reyjane P. Oliveira and colleagues’ 2017 study of the evolutionary trajectory of the Malagasy grass genus <em>Chasechloa</em> instead relied on historical DNA—genomic data incidentally preserved in specimens that are housed in natural history collections—<mark>thus capitalizing on the research potential offered by a vast but hitherto relatively underutilized source of insight into the biological past</mark>.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?</p>","keySource":"solved","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>It explains why the research methodology selected by Oliveira and colleagues is not widely used.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>It specifies potential applications of the approach that Oliveira and colleagues used in their study.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>It offers commentary on the significance of the approach that Oliveira and colleagues used for their study.</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>It emphasizes the importance of Oliveira and colleagues’ findings about the DNA of flora.</p>"}],"correct":"C","rationale":""},{"number":"8","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p><b>Text 1</b><br>Thomas Piketty's book <i>Capital in the Twenty-First Century</i> has a more rigorous structure than its sequel, <i>Capital and Ideology</i>. While first book's chapters all contribute to bolstering a clear, argument about income, the second book's digressions on subjects such as the authorship of the Sanskrit text known as the Manusmriti do not just stretch out the book needlessly but also muddy its reasoning.</p><p><b>Text 2</b><br><i>Capital and Ideology</i> has different aims than Piketty's earlier books. It should be judged not just in the context of Piketty's previous work but placed next to books like Robert Burton's <i>Anatomy of Melancholy</i>, in which theme of the varieties of melancholy is mainly an excuse for a polymath to map his own mind. Even when sections do not explicitly support the central thesis, they link to each other in intriguing ways. None of them should be considered extraneous.</p>","stem":"<p>Based on the texts, the author of Text 1 would most likely agree with the author of Text 2 on which point?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p><i>Capital in the Twenty-First Century</i> book to <i>Capital and Ideology</i>.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>The material in <i>Capital and Ideology</i> on the Manusmriti is essential to the book.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p><i>Capital and Ideology</i> was influenced by the writing of Robert Burton.</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p><i>Capital and Ideology</i> is notably different in structure from some of Piketty's earlier work.</p>"}],"correct":"D","rationale":""},{"number":"9","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"E","stimulus":"<p>Musician and astronomer Darsan Swaroop Bellie researches gravitational waves. These invisible waves move very quickly through space. They cannot be viewed through a telescope, but they do make sounds that can be detected with special equipment. In his musical composition <i>Dance of the Black Holes</i>, Bellie demonstrates what gravitational waves might sound like as two black holes merge in space. With this composition and others, Bellie hopes to make aspects of science more accessible.</p>","stem":"<p>According to the text, what is the subject of Bellie's research?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>Space travel</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>Ocean currents</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>Music history</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>Gravitational waves</p>"}],"correct":"D","rationale":""},{"number":"10","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>The End-Ordovician mass extinction happened approximately 440 million years ago, when about 85 percent of species (including many species of bryozoans) died off. Researchers have proposed the effects of a change in sea temperature as one mechanism that may have brought on this mass extinction. But mass extinctions, while abrupt in geological terms, unfold over thousands or millions of years: it's likely that multiple factors drove widespread species loss.</p>","stem":"<p>Based on the text, the author would most likely agree with which statement about the End-Ordovician mass extinction?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>It likely involved the extinction of more species than is typically believed.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>It occurred over a long period of time and probably had multiple causes.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>It was discovered only recently and is poorly understood.</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>It is hard to detect in Earth's fossil or geological records.</p>"}],"correct":"B","rationale":""},{"number":"11","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from Yung Wing's 1909 memoir <i>My Life in China and America.</i></p><p>We landed in New York on the 12th of April, 1847, after a passage of ninety-eight days of unprecedented fair weather. The New York of 1847 was altogether a different city from the New York of 1909. It was a city of only 250,000 or 300,000 inhabitants; now it is a metropolis rivaling London in population, wealth and commerce. The whole of Manhattan Island is turned into a city of skyscrapers, churches and palatial residences.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main idea of the text?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>The architecture in New York City is more beautiful than that in London.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>Yung has experienced significant personal growth in the time since his arrival to New York City in 1847.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>The journey to New York City was extremely tiring for Yung.</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>New York City has become more developed and populated since Yung's arrival in 1847.</p>"}],"correct":"D","rationale":""},{"number":"12","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p><i>Memoirs of Elleanor Eldridge</i> is an 1838 historical account by Elleanor Eldridge and Frances Harriet Whipple Green. In the book, 