ngs they liked most at higher volumes (greater dB) than recordings they liked less and that musicians tended to listen at higher volumes than nonmusicians did. For example, if the favorite recording of both a participating musician and a participating nonmusician was Jose Gonzalez's “Heartbeats” and the musician played it at 84.8 dB, it was therefore likely that ______ blank</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice most logically completes the text?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>the nonmusician would play \"Heartbeats\" at less than 84.8 dB.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>the nonmusician would play \"Heartbeats\" at greater than 84.8 dB.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>the musician and nonmusician would both play other music by Jose Gonzalez at approximately 84.8 dB.</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>the musician would not play music in the acoustic folk genre at less than 84.8 dB.</p>"}],"correct":"A","rationale":""},{"number":"16","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Right-handedness is overwhelmingly prevalent in humans. Among studies of laterality in nonhuman primates, Dulce D. Shafer's 1988 study of captive gorillas reported no tendency toward right-handedness, while James Welles's 1976 study of captive chimpanzees and catarrhine monkeys did. However, the latter study included only 10 individuals, and a meta-analysis of primate-laterality studies demonstrated that a minimum sample size of 176 individuals is required to be confident that a finding of population-level handedness is not mere statistical noise. The claim of right-handedness in the 1976 study should therefore be treated skeptically given that ______ blank</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice most logically completes the text?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>the study that did not find right-handedness in gorillas was also based on an insufficient population size.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>the apparent difference between the two studies' results may be partly attributable to the 1976 study using a different standard to determine handedness than the 1988 study did.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>the sample size on which the claim is based is far below the threshold identified in the meta-analysis.</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>right-handedness does not occur frequently enough among chimpanzees and catarrhine monkeys to reliably appear in a sample of only 10 individuals.</p>"}],"correct":"C","rationale":""},{"number":"17","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Alabama resident Benjamin S. Turner, one of the nearly two thousand African Americans elected to public office during the decade that followed the Civil War, ______ blank his term as a member of the US House of Representatives in 1871.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>having begun</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>began</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>to begin</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>beginning</p>"}],"correct":"B","rationale":""},{"number":"18","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Olga Oppenheimer and Josephine Paddock were among the 300 artists who exhibited at the 1913 Armory Show, a groundbreaking New York City art exhibition that introduced modernism to American audiences. Marcel Duchamp's abstract cubist aesthetic received the most skepticism from critics, as ______ blank represented a radical departure from the more realistic painting style that was popular at the time.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>it</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>they</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>these</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>we</p>"}],"correct":"A","rationale":""},{"number":"19","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>The International Wheelchair Basketball Federation (IWBF) is one of many sports that collect and analyze data on player performance. Coaches in the IWBF ______ blank these data to help them develop game strategies that have a high probability of success.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>has used</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>use</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>uses</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>is using</p>"}],"correct":"B","rationale":""},{"number":"20","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Polymers used in industrial applications are weakened by environmental stress, mechanical fatigue, and unexpected damage. However, new types of polymers have been engineered to repair ______ blank aided by embedded microcapsules, such materials begin to self-heal.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms of Standard English?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>themselves—upon fracture—</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>themselves upon fracture,</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>themselves. Upon fracture,</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>themselves, upon fracture,</p>"}],"correct":"C","rationale":""},{"number":"21","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>Many past Olympic Games featured demonstration sports—nonmedal events—to showcase sports related to the host country. These events included glíma, a combat sport popular in Sweden, and bandy, a hockey-like sport popular in Norway. ______ blank they were chosen as demonstration sports at the Olympic Games in Stockholm, Sweden, and Oslo, Norway, respectively.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>Additionally,</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>Fittingly,</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>By contrast,</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"}],"correct":"B","rationale":""},{"number":"22","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>In Amarna, Egypt, archaeologist Anna Hodgkinson unearthed bits of glass near lower-status dwellings, which she believes may refute the long-held notion that the material was enjoyed exclusively by Ancient Egyptian royalty. _____ archaeologist Thilo Rehren states flatly that glass doesn't appear to have been \"a closely controlled royal commodity,\" concurring, based on his own research, that the material was more common than once surmised.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>As such,</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>Nonetheless,</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>Consequently,</p>"},{"label":"D","content":"<p>Likewise,</p>"}],"correct":"D","rationale":""},{"number":"23","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Documentary TV programs in the slow TV genre consist of uninterrupted broadcasts of ordinary events in real time.</li><li>MORA: Zeichner is a German slow TV program.</li><li>The 45-minute-long program documented an artist making a pencil drawing during a train journey.</li><li>It first aired in 2016.</li><li>Slow TV has been called \"the world's most boring television.\"</li><li>American journalist Nathan Heller praises it, writing that “it affords a visceral kind of armchair tourism.\"</li></ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to use a quotation to refute the claim that slow TV programs are boring. Which choice most effectively uses relevant 