38 wood ducks visited, the researchers found that the younger ducks tended to visit more nest boxes than the older ducks.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>The researchers investigated each nesting site for signs that it had been visited by the female wood ducks.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>By recording how many nest boxes each duck visited, the researchers discovered that only a relatively small percentage (13.0%) of the ducks visited 10 or more nest boxes.</p>"}],"correct":"B","rationale":""},{"number":"26","section":"Reading and Writing","module":1,"format":"mc","difficulty":"M","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jaume Bertran was a fifteenth-century Majorcan cartographer of portolan charts.</li><li>Francesco Beccari was a fifteenth-century Genoese cartographer of portolan charts.</li><li>Portolan charts were early nautical charts that mapped the waterways of the Mediterranean and Black Seas.</li><li>Portolan charts in the Genoese tradition tended to be sparse in illustrations.</li><li>Those in the Majorcan tradition tended to be richly illustrated.</li><li>In Majorcan charts, the Alps are depicted as a chicken's foot, and the Tagus River is depicted as a shepherd's crook.</li></ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to make a distinction between the two portolan traditions. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","keySource":"paper","choices":[{"label":"A","content":"<p>While portolan charts in the Majorcan tradition tended to be richly illustrated, those in the Genoese tradition mapped the waterways of the Mediterranean and Black Seas.</p>"},{"label":"B","content":"<p>Being in the Majorcan tradition, the portolan charts of Jaume Bertran differed from those of the Genoese cartographer Francesco Beccari.</p>"},{"label":"C","content":"<p>Unlike Genoese portolan charts, which could include illustrations of chicken feet and shepherds' crooks, Majorc